  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 113 PM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nA surface ridge of high pressure will settle south into the area, \nbringing another morning of cool temperatures. Expect Friday morning \nlows from the upper teens to lower 20s in most locations. Most of \nthe area near and east of the James River into southwest MN and \nnorthwest Iowa will see a 30-35% chance for temperatures below 20.\n\nCool high pressure slowly shifts east on Friday, bring southerly \nwinds into central SD and lighter east to southeast winds near and \neast of Highway 81. Highs will remain below normal, topping out from \nthe upper 30s to lower 40s.\n\nLow temperatures will rebound a bit Saturday morning as high \npressure shifts east. Areas east of I-29 will see the best chance to \ndip into the lower 20s again, while southerly flow will slowly \nincrease through the night. Lows in central SD will drop to 25 to \n30, and possibly warm through the night. \n\nSaturday into Sunday will see milder temperatures, highs mainly \nlower 40s to lower 50s, but this will be a bit off set by the \nstronger southerly winds, likely gusting to 25 to 35 mph both days.\n\nMild air overspreads the area early next week as a wave deepens to \nthe west Tuesday night into Wednesday. This will keep southerly flow \nin the low levels in place during this time, along with breezy \nconditions. Highs will mainly be in the upper 40s to mid 50s while \nlows only fall into the mid 30s to lower 40s.\n\nThe next better chance for precipitation will come after the end of \nthis 7 day forecast cycle, Wednesday night into Thursday. Still\ntoo early for any details but given the placement of the mid and\nupper level low pressure suspect any winter weather hazards \nwill be west and north of the area with a more showery concern \nin the local area as the jet/dry slot wraps north Wednesday \nnight into Thursday.",
